id: pm-9c7h9x
title: "Continuous invariant fuzzing: randomized operation sequences checked against declared workspace, history, and graph invariants"
description: "The suite proves that specified operations produce specified results. It does not systematically attack the space of operation SEQUENCES, which is where a data-integrity engine actually fails: an interleaving of create, close, restore, redact, compact, merge, schema change, and config change that leaves a hash chain unverifiable, an edge pointing at a tombstone, a derived index disagreeing with authoritative files, or a claim held by nobody but not released. Declare the invariants that must hold after any sequence — the hash chain verifies; every declared edge resolves or is explicitly a tombstone reference; derived artifacts agree with authoritative files or are marked stale; lifecycle state is reachable from the recorded history; no item is unreconstructable from its stream — and then generate randomized sequences against them, with shrinking so a failure produces a minimal reproducer and a seed that reproduces it exactly. This complements rather than duplicates the seeded fault and concurrency harness: that harness injects failures into interleavings, this one explores operation sequences under normal conditions. Every discovered violation becomes a filed item with its minimal reproducer as a permanent regression fixture."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags[5]: ci,integrity,property-testing,quality,testing
created_at: "2026-07-25T12:31:35.988Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T12:35:41.275Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "The invariant set is declared explicitly as data — chain verifiability, edge resolvability, derived-artifact agreement, lifecycle reachability, per-item reconstructability — with each invariant naming what violates it; Randomized sequences cover create, update, close, restore, delete, redact, compact, merge, schema change, and config change in arbitrary orders; A violation produces a minimal shrunk reproducer plus a seed that reproduces it deterministically; Every violation found is filed as an item with its reproducer added to the permanent regression corpus, linked discovered_from this item; The suite runs on a schedule with a time budget rather than blocking every change, and a violation opens work immediately rather than being retried; Coverage over the declared invariant set is reported, so an invariant no sequence has ever attacked is visible as a gap"
goal: project management = context management
objective: The engine's invariants are attacked continuously by sequences no author would think to write
value: "Every claim pm makes — immutable history, restorable state, verifiable chains, correct graphs — is an invariant claim, and invariant claims are only as strong as the adversary that has tested them"
impact: "Adds a long-running randomized suite whose failures are, by construction, real integrity defects; requires the invariant set to be declared explicitly for the first time"
outcome: "Integrity defects are found by machine before a workspace hits them, with a minimal reproducer attached"
parent: pm-33cw
risk: medium
confidence: 65
